\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Research architecture. Cleaning and polarity create one eligible candidate source, after which the analysis deliberately separates two objects. H1 evaluates every eligible candidate at fixed notional through $T_{end}-1$. The CEM branch selects and sizes overlapping candidates under capital constraints; T1--T4 modify fitness, chronology, sizing, and allocation, respectively. H1 output does not feed the portfolio results.}}{6}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{4}{6}{Research architecture. Cleaning and polarity create one eligible candidate source, after which the analysis deliberately separates two objects. H1 evaluates every eligible candidate at fixed notional through $T_{end}-1$. The CEM branch selects and sizes overlapping candidates under capital constraints; T1--T4 modify fitness, chronology, sizing, and allocation, respectively. H1 output does not feed the portfolio results}{figure.caption.15}{}}
